/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/23/code.py:23:#    - Example trace: a down-right L could visit bg cells (4,4),(5,5), step onto portal A at (6,6),
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/23/code.py:24:#      emerge at A'=(11,3), continue to (12,4), then step onto portal B at (13,5), emerge at B'=(3,12),
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/23/code.py:30:#    - Two portal pairs are enough to make multi-warp paths possible without cluttering the 16x16 board.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/23/code.py:31:#    - The generator forces at least one blue collision created by portal-using rays and at least one ray
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/23/code.py:32:#      with two or more portal hops. That keeps the portal mechanic central rather than cosmetic.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/23/code.py:33:#    - Sprite colors and portal colors are drawn from a small shared palette excluding output-only colors
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/409aa875/23/code.py:37:#    - Original solver assumption "every non-bg component is a triangle" is broken by singleton portals,
